  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Another cold morning in store for central PA. \nFrost Advisory in place for some of our Eastern counties.\n\nHigh pressure will continue to slide east today, with winds \nshifting around to the SW. A frost advisory is in place for the \nportions of Eastern PA in the Middle Susquehanna Valley where \nconditions are expected to line up the best for frost.\n\n\n-------------------------------------------------------------\n \nKEY MESSAGE 2: Extended stretch of dry and seasonal Fall \nweather this week, followed by a chance of rain on Sunday into \nMonday.\n\nHigh confidence in a prolonged stretch of dry and seasonable \nFall weather this week. Expect cool nights and refreshing \nafternoons with low humidity through Saturday. Wednesday cannot \nrule out an isolated shower or two, especially in northwestern \nPA as a cold front moves into the area, but rainfall totals will\nbe insignificant. A tropical system in the gulf will move up \nnorth towards the Ohio River Valley this weekend bringing \ntropical moisture and rain potential Sunday afternoon into \nMonday. This system looks fairly progressive. However, robust \nforcing and PWATs in the 1.5-1.75\" range, particularly in the \nsouthern tier of the state, may yield some periods of heavy \nrain. Uncertainty remains regarding how this system plays out.",
